REPORT 1: BUG 10 RESOLUTION REPORT (features/prompt-manager.js)
1. Root Cause Analysis
In features/prompt-manager.js, the updateVariant(promptId, variantId, name, payload) method evaluated non-append variant updates using:
variant.content = payload.content ? payload.content.trim() : '';
When a caller submitted an edit payload with an empty string, whitespace-only content, or a missing payload.content property, the condition evaluated to false and assigned "" to variant.content. This erased the existing prompt variant content without warning.
Additionally, init() initialized this.prompts in memory via this.getDefaultPrompts() when chrome.storage.local returned empty on initial launch, but failed to invoke this.save(). As a result, default prompts were lost if storage was inspected or cleared before a user performed a write action.
2. Architectural Solution & Structural Changes
Guarded Content Updating (updateVariant):
Check property types explicitly (typeof payload.content === 'string').
Preserve existing variant.content if the incoming payload is empty or whitespace-only. Fall back to parent prompt.content if variant.content was previously unassigned.
Apply equivalent type guards for append-mode variants (payload.addition).
First-Launch Persistence (init):
Invoke this.save() immediately upon populating this.getDefaultPrompts() during first-run initialization for both chrome.storage.local and localStorage backends.
3. Verification & Edge-Case Testing
Empty Payload Test: Submitting an update payload with content: "" retains existing non-empty variant text.
Partial Update Test: Updating a variant name without providing a payload object preserves existing content and addition properties intact.
Initial Install Test: Invoking init() on an uninitialized storage state creates default storage keys containing the initial FZFD directive prompt.
REPORT 2: BUG 11 RESOLUTION REPORT (features/zip-processor.js)
1. Root Cause Analysis
Path sanitization was duplicated across parseTargetInfo, isPathHeaderLine, updateStagedFile, stageZip, stageMultipleFiles, and stageRawText. Each location performed naive regex replacements and checked parts.includes('..') after splitting on forward slashes (/).
This implementation was vulnerable to padded or obfuscated path inputs:
Inputs containing spaces around parent directory relative syntax (such as path/to/.. /file.js or path/to/ .. /file.js) split into ".. " or " ..". Exact equality checks against '..' failed, allowing malformed path parts to pass sanitization.
Folders with leading or trailing whitespace (path / to / file.js) produced directory handles containing trailing spaces, causing DOMExceptions during File System Access API operations.
Dot-only directory segments (path/to/.../file.js) were not recognized as invalid relative directory references.
2. Architectural Solution & Structural Changes
A centralized path sanitization method sanitizePathParts(rawPath) was integrated into ZipProcessor:
UTF-8 BOM Stripping & Input Trimming: Strips leading Byte Order Marks (\uFEFF) and trims surrounding whitespace.
Illegal Character Substitution & Slash Normalization: Replaces illegal OS characters (:, *, ?, ", <, >, |) with _, converts backslashes (\) to forward slashes (/), and collapses duplicate slashes (/+/).
Segment-Level Trimming & Filtering: Splits paths into raw segments, applies .trim() to every segment, and filters out empty strings and single dot (.) self-references.
Traversal & Dot-Only Segment Detection: Iterates through every trimmed segment. Rejects the path if any segment equals '..' or matches dot-only patterns (/^\.+$/).
Clean Path Reconstruction: Recombines sanitized directory parts and filename into a clean relative display path ([...parts, fileName].join('/')).
3. Verification & Edge-Case Testing
Space-Padded Parent Traversal Test: path/to/.. /file.js and path/to/ .. /file.js are caught and rejected with a explicit traversal exception.
Dot-Sequence Test: path/to/.../file.js is identified as an invalid dot-only directory reference and rejected.
Padded Path Normalization Test: src / components / UserProfile.jsx is cleanly normalized to src/components/UserProfile.jsx with directory parts ['src', 'components'] and filename 'UserProfile.jsx'.
Clean Fallback Test: Multi-file drops and ZIP archive entries without line 1 comment directives run through sanitizePathParts before disk handle creation, ensuring invalid archive paths fail gracefully during staging.
REPORT 3: BUG 12 RESOLUTION REPORT (content.js)
1. Root Cause Analysis
In renderStagingMatrix inside content.js:
The master overwrite checkbox (#masterToggle) set chk.checked on visible checkboxes when clicked, but masterToggle.checked state was never updated when users toggled individual file row checkboxes (.fibo-replace-check) or filtered rows using the search box (#stagingSearch).
If a user filtered the list, selected all visible overwrites, cleared the search, and then unchecked an item, masterToggle remained checked, misleading the user about the true batch state.
The UI lacked an indeterminate state representation (masterToggle.indeterminate) when a subset of visible files was selected for overwrite.
2. Architectural Solution & Structural Changes
Centralized Master State Synchronization (updateMasterToggleState):
Queries all .fibo-replace-check elements whose parent row is currently visible (row.style.display !== 'none').
Evaluates visible checkboxes:
If all visible items are checked, masterToggle.checked = true and masterToggle.indeterminate = false.
If some visible items are checked, masterToggle.checked = false and masterToggle.indeterminate = true.
If no visible items are checked (or no visible items exist), masterToggle.checked = false and masterToggle.indeterminate = false.
Event Binding Integration:
Invokes updateMasterToggleState() on stagingSearch.oninput during row filtering.
Binds onchange = updateMasterToggleState to every individual .fibo-replace-check checkbox.
Calls updateMasterToggleState() immediately after initial matrix rendering and after master toggle click events.
3. Verification & Edge-Case Testing
Individual Check Toggle Test: Unchecking a single file row among five checked rows automatically converts masterToggle.checked to false and sets masterToggle.indeterminate to true.
Search Filter Synchronization Test: Filtering the matrix down to 2 files and checking both updates masterToggle.checked to true. Clearing the search filter recalculates total visible items and sets masterToggle.indeterminate to true (since hidden items remain unchecked).
Zero Results Test: Typing a search query that matches no staged files sets masterToggle.checked = false and masterToggle.indeterminate = false without throwing DOM query errors.
